{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Recorded what the target's own tests do and do not cover in this area, using the test files as sources. The RestoreCommittedLogs tests build a single-node cluster, commit commands, snapshot, restart and assert only that the FSM is replayed up to the stored commit index (and that an incompatible log store is rejected); none of them constructs a restart whose last snapshot predates a committed configuration entry, and none observes the configuration the restarted node ends up with. The user-restore path is covered by snapshotAndRestore, which asserts the FSM is reverted to the snapshot and that all nodes agree. This is a sourced observation about existing coverage, not a new gate or contract, and it does not change any conclusion.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-test-restorecommitted\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft_test.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1183,\\\"end_line\\\":1279,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"test_expectation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-test-userrestore\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft_test.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1633,\\\"end_line\\\":1700,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"test_expectation\\\"}],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@existing_test_coverage\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"The repository's own tests for Config.RestoreCommittedLogs exercise a single-node cluster that commits commands, takes a snapshot and restarts the node, asserting only that the FSM is replayed up to the log store's commit index and that the commit index sits between the snapshot index and the last log index; no test constructs a restart whose snapshot predates a committed configuration entry, and none observes the configuration or quorum the restarted node uses. The user-restore path is covered by snapshotAndRestore, which